From 5eaf421b8e21202a83c0f7f146c3be334f438be0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Roessner <c@roessner.co>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 12:39:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] cleanup: accept DSN evidence only on private service

A Milter cannot trust DSN origin data that arrived as message content or
through the public cleanup service. Such input can be supplied by an SMTP
client or by another untrusted submission path.

Add a private dsn_cleanup master service and a post_mail interface that
passes the original queue ID and encoded original envelope as transient
attributes. The cleanup server recognizes those reserved attributes only
when invoked as dsn_cleanup. It rejects them on other services, rejects
duplicates and malformed or incomplete input, and does not write them to
the new queue file.

The existing public cleanup service and post_mail interfaces are unchanged.
Systems that do not use dsn_cleanup see no behavioral or protocol change.

Add positive and negative cleanup tests for trusted input, public-service
input, duplicates, incomplete input, and non-base64url input.

Tested with:

    make -C src/cleanup test_cleanup_envelope
    make -j4
